---
title: "Evolution"
note: "A creature that evolves one trait at a time, for ever. Each clip is a generation: one of its body, skin, limbs or eyes changes ($change) and the rest stays as it was ($body~1 …). Now and then (6%) it spins a cocoon and climbs out as something entirely new. The world is rolled once per seed (dial $world). GOTO lines steer it; the traits come with the preset (@lib). Run (Instant) plays it until you stop."
tags: [loops, h3, reel, goto, nature, motion_context]
---
@h3 t2va 16:9
context: 22
style: nature documentary, macro photography, soft natural light, one continuous shot
$world = {a tide pool among black rocks|a rainforest floor of wet leaves|a desert of red sand at dusk|the clear ice of a frozen lake}
MUSIC: a slow, curious marimba at a soft volume

@lib evo_bodies
  a body like a soft glass bead
  a long segmented body
  a round, armoured body
  a slender body balanced on a long tail
@lib evo_skins
  translucent skin that glows faintly blue
  mottled green scales
  velvet black fur
  iridescent feathers
  ridged amber plates
@lib evo_limbs
  six thin jointed legs
  two broad paddle fins
  a ring of soft tentacles
  a pair of delicate wings
@lib evo_eyes
  a single huge dark eye
  a row of tiny bright eyes
  eyes on long stalks
  no eyes at all, only quivering feelers

CHUNK the origin
$body = __evo_bodies__
$skin = __evo_skins__
$limbs = __evo_limbs__
$eyes = __evo_eyes__
SHOT 8s: push in, slow
On $world, a small creature stirs for the first time: it has $body, $skin, $limbs and $eyes. It tests its limbs and creeps forward into the light.
SFX: a soft wet click; the faint rustle of its first steps
HANDOFF: the creature pauses, perfectly still

CHUNK the generations
$change = {body|skin|limbs|eyes}
$body = {? $change[body]: __evo_bodies__|$body~1}
$skin = {? $change[skin]: __evo_skins__|$skin~1}
$limbs = {? $change[limbs]: __evo_limbs__|$limbs~1}
$eyes = {? $change[eyes]: __evo_eyes__|$eyes~1}
$leap = {6% leap}
SHOT 8s: static
A generation later, on $world, the creature has changed: it has $body, $skin, $limbs and $eyes.
? $change[body]: It stretches its new body slowly, as if getting used to its size.
? $change[skin]: The light plays over its new skin as it turns.
? $change[limbs]: It tries its new limbs clumsily, then with growing confidence.
? $change[eyes]: It blinks and looks around as if seeing for the first time.
SFX: soft rustling; a quiet chirp
HANDOFF: the creature pauses, perfectly still
? $leap[leap]: GOTO: the metamorphosis
GOTO: the generations

CHUNK the metamorphosis
$body = __evo_bodies__
$skin = __evo_skins__
$limbs = __evo_limbs__
$eyes = __evo_eyes__
SHOT 10s: push in, slow
On $world, the creature curls up and spins itself into a glowing cocoon. The cocoon trembles and splits, and out climbs something new: it has $body, $skin, $limbs and $eyes.
SFX: a low hum rising; silk tearing slowly
HANDOFF: the new creature pauses, perfectly still
GOTO: the generations
